                { author: "Clarisse", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-19", text: "This is a great great way to explore what Hoi An really is. We saw the dying cultural traditions in the area, which is sad, but really makes you appreciate the totality of Hoi An. Cycling across the countryside lets you experience and really see how locals live their day to day. Would really recommend this tour esp to peoplr who wanted to immerse in the culture of Hoi An. This is a must!!" },
                { author: "Dana", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-19", text: "Tam was an excellent guide. He was very knowledgeable about the history and culture, and I learned a lot during the tour. It was great being able to immerse ourselves in the local culture. I think the small group size was perfect because we could all interact comfortably. One thing to be mindful of if you're under 5\" is that the bike won't be as comfortable. You'll be tiptoeing on stops unless you're able to get close to the curb. It was terribly hot when we had our tour and I almost gave up at the end when we passed the bridges, but Tam was kind and considerate, and the other people I was wit" }
