  'fansipan-mountain-trek-indochina-s-highest-peak-2-days': {
            averageRating: 4.72,
            totalReviews: 94,
            guideRating: 4.75,
            valueRating: 4.21,
            reviews: [
                { author: "John", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-28", text: "Having trekked Fansipan in day previously, we wanted to do the overnight trek to try and catch the sunrise. The hike itself was easier over the two days as you’d expect. Staying at Camp 2 was tough. The guide, Minh, who was helpful and patient throughout, cooked a great meal but the camping shed was hard going. You MUST bring your own pillow…I suggest an inflatable one like my partner had the foresight to pack. It was also surprisingly noisy with other trekkers and guides listening to Social Media until the early hours…given that we were getting up at 4.00am it made sleeping very difficult. Bu" },
                { author: "Esther", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-03", text: "Back to basic, back to nature! A great way to disconnect. The guides were top-notch and eating together at basecamp created such a vibe. Pro tip: Don't underestimate the temperature drop! Bring extra layers and a reliable headlight for the final ascent in the dark." },
                { author: "Albert", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-01-20", text: "Hiking to Fansipan with Nomad Trails is well worth the price. They handled the transportation between Lao Cai and Sapa seamlessly in both directions. My guide, Cha, was super! Not only did he guide me along the trail, but he also proved to be a wonderful source of insight into Vietnamese culture." },
                { author: "Stefan", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-12-20", text: "Had a great time, amazing guide! The ascent is challenging, but if you’re in a. Small group it will be much faster than advertised. In the Base camp can be COLD, so come prepared. Other than that - beautiful and very rewarding experience!" },
                { author: "Jasmine", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-08-25", text: "loved every minute - it was raining pretty heavy but our guide kept our spirits up. Would highly recommend!!!!! A memory from Vietnam that will last forever" },
                { author: "Timothy", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-07-18", text: "Great! Dress warm with a windproof as the summit and nights drop to 2-3 degrees. The tour guide said I would be fine in my sweater. I was not fine, but I had a great time anyway." },
                { author: "Adam", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-05-07", text: "The trek was amazing with a local guide that made it more memorable. My guide was a superstar and was always checking that I was ok and pointing out points of interest. Stopping many times along the way to take in the views and also taking photos. Lunch, dinner, breakfast were all cooked up by my guide and it was awesome. A selection of dishes all different and just a real taste of Vietnams region. My guide was super fit , scaling these rocky treks like a mountain goat, and one of the most friendly and accommodating you’ll find. We were able to stumble across many great places and experiences" },
                { author: "Maluleka", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-05-01", text: "The experience was great and my guide Sinh was truly phenomenal." },
                { author: "Juliette", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-03-03", text: "It was really nice and the sunset was just magic !" },
                { author: "Louis", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-02-17", text: "Hezekiah was an amazing guide. He was very friendly and helpful during the tour. Would definitely do it again!" },
                { author: "Garion", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2023-12-21", text: "Highly recommend. Well organised value for money. My guide Tong was great. Particularly enjoyed the authenticity of the overnight with other guides and tourists we all ate together a great meal they prepared over a fire. The views were great when we had rare breaks in the clouds. Great experience even though the summit was clouded in." },
                { author: "Rodney", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2023-08-19", text: "Embarking on the challenging trek led by an amazing guide was an adventure of a lifetime that left me in awe at every step. The breathtaking landscapes, the camaraderie among fellow trekkers, and the guidance of our knowledgeable guide made this experience truly exceptional. The anticipation of watching the world awaken from such an incredible vantage point filled us with excitement. However, one lesson learned during this trek is that even the most well-prepared adventurers can encounter unexpected challenges. When the moment came to head out to witness the sunrise , the absence of adequate l" }
            ]
        },
