  'sapa-3-day-trek-hidden-villages-and-nature-with-mama-shushu-by-local-operator': {
            averageRating: 5.0,
            totalReviews: 8,
            guideRating: 5.0,
            valueRating: 5.0,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Ioanna", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-09-07", text: "Thank you very much to Mama Shu Shu and Mimi for this warm welcome. They are both so kind and loving. We spent three exceptional days, whether during the day with Mimi, or even in the evenings spent with her and Mama Shu Shu. What we really enjoyed was talking with them and learning a lot of things about the culture of Vietnam and, more particularly, about their village. We were welcomed like kings and quickly felt at home. Thank you for this experience that will remain forever engraved in our memories. If the opportunity arises, we will come back with great pleasure. <3 Luna, Jules, Julien &" },
                { author: "Ashley", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-09-01", text: "Mama Shushu and her daughters were so loving, kind, & welcoming. I had such an amazing time at their homestay! One of the best experiences I have had during my time in Vietnam." },
                { author: "Andrea", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-20", text: "We had three fantastic days with Mama Shushu and her family. Her daughter Mimi went hiking with us, and we were able to discover so much and get to know the culture. It’s not just an activity—it’s so much more. Mama Shushu is such a warm-hearted woman who gives it her all. The tour was superbly organized, everything went smoothly, and we even cooked together! Thank you for this fantastic experience! I can highly recommend it!!! Andrea and Timur<3" },
                { author: "Hilary", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-14", text: "Mama ShuShu, Yaya, and Hwu were such excellent guides and hosts! The homestay is in a very beautiful, mountainous area of Sapa, surrounded completely by nature. Mama ShuShu is so generous and makes you feel at home with her family. The trekking is intense but so worth it! (there are also more gentle routes if needed, though we did not take them)." },
                { author: "Choukri", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-09", text: "Had an amazing time with mama Susu and the family. Mama Susu was a great host and made us feel at home. During the day we hiked through the rice fields and mountains of Sa Pa. Mimi was a great guide." },
                { author: "S", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-09", text: "I did the 3-day hike with Mama Shushu, and it was honestly one of the best experiences I’ve had in Vietnam. Mama Shushu is one of the most loving and caring people I’ve met here. She and her family made me feel so welcome from the very beginning, and I felt great the entire time — both while trekking and staying at the homestay. One of my favorite moments was on the second day when I joined them in preparing dinner. We had such a fun time together, and I have to mention the French fries… they are absolutely to die for. You’ll understand once you try them yourself — I ate an insane amount of th" },
                { author: "Verena", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-12", text: "Wenn ihr in das Leben in einem Hmong-Dorf eintauchen wollt, dann besucht unbedingt Mama Shushu. die Trekkingtouren habe ich mit ihrer Tochter Yaya gemacht und beide haben tolle (auch persönliche) Einblicke in ihre Welt und das Leben in den Bergen bei Sapa gegeben. Mama Shushu hat zudem den Zusatz Mama ganz klar verdient, sie kümmert sich um ihre Gäste ganz wunderbar. Das Essen bei Mama Shushu war ebenfalls ganz hervorragend. Alles in allem waren die 3 Tage ein ganz außergewöhnlicher Fall von Glück. Insbesondere Mama Shushu und Yaya, aber auch der ganzen Familie, wünsche ich von Herzen alles Li" }
            ]
        },
