  'love-silver-waterfall-lonelytree-in-heaven-rice-field-in-sapa': {
            averageRating: 4.96,
            totalReviews: 37,
            guideRating: 5.0,
            valueRating: 4.62,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Jordan", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-09-11", text: "All of the activities in this booking were great! May was a great guide and spoke very good English. It was rainy the first half of the day, but that didn’t majorly impact the day by any means. The picnic lunch was also very good! Would recommend." },
                { author: "Jade", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-05-10", text: "We booked this tour while in sapa. we loved everything about this from the walk , home made lunch and our guide was phenomenal we had Mo she was so engaging and went above and beyond to make our adventure exciting , we would 10000% recommend this tour to anyone ." },
                { author: "Tim", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-11-10", text: "We had a local guide who could speak good english and provided us with a lot of Information during the trip. It was possible to change the planned route to have fewer walking distance since we didn‘t feel so well on that day. Because of the change we paid 350.000 VND more because the we ate at a local restaurant (really good and plenty food) and the car had to pick us up a longer distance away. The transport was well organized and comfortable. We had a little rain and very misty weather but that can happen if you travel in november. We liked the trip a lot and you get to see many places in a f" },
                { author: "Lukas", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-11-09", text: "I had a great time. Waterfalls are amazing (especially Love waterfall) and in good weather (which was today) you can have breathtaking views from the Lonely Tree. Then the hike takes you down the hill through villages and if you take \"natural\" path, you will have great views over rice fields. Ms Mo did a great job as a guide and I learnt a lot about the places and culture." },
                { author: "Frederick", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-07-03", text: "The landscape was very beautiful. Easy trek than can be done whatever the shape you're in!" },
                { author: "Brian", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-06-12", text: "Our one-day visit to Sapa was significantly enriched by this fantastic tour. Mr. Tinh from Sapa Original Trek was incredibly helpful and communicative throughout the planning process. Our tour guide, Ms. Mu, was delightful, knowledgeable, and friendly, providing detailed insights into each location we visited. The tour was filled with awe-inspiring natural beauty, including stunning waterfalls, majestic views, rice terraces, and charming local villages. Although it was rainy and hazy for half of our day, this actually enhanced the experience, leading to gushing waterfalls and spectacular photo" },
                { author: "Bella", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-06-07", text: "We had the BEST time! Our tour guide took us to the two waterfalls and then on a long trekk down the mountain and through the villages. Halfway down we stopped for a picnic where he cut up pineapple, watermelon, cucumber, tomato etc and made us homemade Bahn Mi with chicken he cooked that morning. We loved hearing about his upbringing (be sure to ask about school, cooking, and the Buffalo incident if you have Sing as your tour guide)! And the scenery was beautiful!" },
                { author: "Timothy", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-04-08", text: "Sinh was a fantastic guide. Very knowledgeable, even with flora and fauna--petting local buffalo on the trek to Love Waterfall. He also shared stories from his home tribe and details of his personal life which were so very interesting and inspiring. It's a walking tour so bring good shoes! We wore the wrong shoes but the tour operator was excellent and flexible when we needed to make changes during the tour. Large water and a/c car was provided so the whole experience was well planned. Highly recommend." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-14", text: "Sehr gut! Sehr viel erlebt und in die Welt der Dörfer eingetaucht. Kann ich nur empfehlen." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-17", text: "Our guide, Mo, spoke good English and took great care of our family, with two children aged 13 and 10. She patiently guided us through the at-times challenging village roads and rice fields. We were allowed to go at our own pace and Love Waterfall was simply amazing and spectacular. All in, this private tour is very value for money!" },
                { author: "Lydia", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-10", text: "Wir hatten zwei wunderbare Wanderungen und können die Tour uneingeschränkt weiterempfehlen. Wir sind schon sehr früh mit dem Nachtbus in Sa Pa eingetroffen und wurden trotzdem herzlich empfangen. Uns wurde ein Zimmer zur Verfügung gestellt, in dem wir uns noch etwas hinlegen und uns frisch machen konnten. Unser Wander Guide Cho hat uns super geführt und uns mit vielen Infos versorgt. Auch die Übernachtung im Homestay war gut und authentisch. Wir wurden zur Abreise sogar zum Busbahnhof gebracht. Alles in allem eine tolle Tour mit Rundumbetreuung. Würden wir wieder so buchen." },
                { author: "Dirk", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-09-17", text: "Super Tour können wir zu 100% empfehlen. Wir sind mit dem Nachtbus von Hanoi nach Sa Pa gefahren und konnten dann zu Fuß von der Bus Station zum Büro der Organisation rüber laufen. Trotz der frühen Uhrzeit 6:00 wurden wir hier sehr freundlich empfangen und konnten direkt auf ein Zimmer und noch ein bisschen schlafen bis die Tour gestartet ist. Das Zimmer stand uns den ganzen Tag zur Verfügung, so das wir unsere Sachen dort lassen konnten und nur unseren Wanderrucksack mitgenommen haben. Dann ging’s los in einen wunderschönen Tag mit May! Haben verschiedene Wasserfälle und herrliche Aussichtspu" }
            ]
        },
