  'private-tour-to-long-tan-former-australian-military-base-in-ho-chi-minh-city': {
            averageRating: 4.79,
            totalReviews: 15,
            guideRating: 5.0,
            valueRating: 4.25,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Andrew", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-28", text: "Trip was fantastic. Alex was so knowledgeable and was able toto show us everything we wanted to see. Anyone planning a trip to Long Tan area, I would highly recommend this tour." },
                { author: "Peter", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-14", text: "Excellent private tour with our tour guide Vinnie, who was very knowledgeable. Would recommend this tour to anyone who would like to do this. Also a chance meeting Australian diggers that served there made the experience special." },
                { author: "Rachael", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-08", text: "Our guide Lucky was brilliant. Made the trip interesting and fun. Our driver Boo was awesome too. Very good tour for Australian and New Zealand tourists who are interested in this part of history." },
                { author: "Michelle", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-04-06", text: "Vinney, our guide, was excellent. He was so informative, not just about Australian war history in Vietnam, but also about Vietnam history, economics, politics and sights to visit. The tour was just long enough. It was great not to be on a big bus tour. Not sure of if I needed to hear the Australian National anthem when paying respects at the memorial (but others may like it)." },
                { author: "peter", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2023-10-17", text: "A great trip. Tuan was a fantastic guide and had a great knowledge of the battle. Definitely worth going on if you have any interest in Australian Military history" },
                { author: "Anne", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2023-02-28", text: "Tuan, our guide, was fabulous. He was a really excellent guide, having had firsthand experience of the Vietnam War. He shared his experiences as well as the history associated with the war. Definitely would recommend this tour for all Australians visiting HCMC." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2023-06-10", text: "Tuan was an amazing guide, given that he is a Veteran of the war, he had incredible insight and information that came firsthand and it added a very deep level of immersion. Couldn't recommend it higher, please do yourself a favour and seek him out for all your war related tours." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 4, date: "2023-03-10", text: "The airfield is long gone, turned into a quarry no point going out there. Going to to the vetrans school was also a watse of time. No scheduled rest room breaks for females, as the men jist go onthe side of the back roads." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2022-07-30", text: "This is a tour for all Australians and New Zealanders visiting Vietnam. We have no personal connections to the Independence War. Alex, our guide, was personable, knowledgeable and flexible. His indepth knowledge the Long Tan area helped us to “see” the area where the Australian and NZ troops were based and where the battle for Long Tan took place. We were deeply moved by the ceremony he curated at the Long Tan memorial - Alex understands the significance to Australians and was respectful. Depending on the traffic, it’s a 2 hour+ trip from Ho Chi Minh City. Recommended." },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2022-07-30", text: "Fantastic private tour with very knowledgeable and experienced guide (Phi). It was great to stand in the footsteps of the Australian Army and especially the guys at Long Tan. Well worth the experience to be a part of Australian and South Vietnamese history." }
            ]
        },
