                { author: "Ben", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-10-10", text: "The Saigon Sniper range turned out to be one of the most surprising things I did in Ho Chi Minh City. My friend and I booked the transfer, and the calm, friendly driver set the tone for the day. The range was clean, safe, and well-run, with staff who explained everything clearly. We chose 100 bullets for an hour, which was plenty. The first few shots were shocking, but soon it felt strangely grounding, even meditative. What stood out most was how respectful and supportive the instructors were. As two queer travelers, it felt good to be in a space that could have felt intimidating but didn’t. I" }
