  'cu-chi-tunnels-small-group-tour-and-war-veteran': {
            averageRating: 4.64,
            totalReviews: 356,
            guideRating: 4.5,
            valueRating: 4.62,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Sophie", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-29", text: "We had an absolutely brilliant day - our guide Sunny was great, she knew so much history to share with us and had lots of facts, answering all of our questions, she was an excellent tour guide. The tunnels are a truly great experience and we would highly recommend this specific tour - lots of other tour groups appeared to be in very large groups but this tour only does small groups, in fact we were the only two people on our tour!! We were picked up and dropped off right outside our hotel. Sunny also gave us lots of great tips for the rest of our trip, and we are so grateful!" },
                { author: "Mariam", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-01-13", text: "Our full day trip was great!! Not a huge group to travel with so it makes things much more relaxed (about 9 people). We started early but finished early as well (2PM) which helped escape the afternoon rush. The Cu Chi tunnels were tougher to go through than expected but there are many exits for one to leave if things get claustrophobic 👍. The highlight for me was meeting the war veteran who was really open to everyone’s questions 😊. Our guide was friendly, informative and patient with everyone wanting to try different things. 10/10 would definitely recommend this activity!!" },
                { author: "Phil", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-01-13", text: "100% recommend going to the tunnels and meeting the veteran, overall an incredible experience that was immersive and emotional. Sunny our guide was absolutely brilliant! She was super friendly, knowledgeable, and despite giving the tour thousands of times her guidance was energetic, engaged, adaptive to our questions and areas of interest (i.e. we never felt stuck in a routine path that was well worn). We even had time to enjoy a great coffee stop at a local (truly) place with her and thoroughly enjoyed the conversation." },
                { author: "Claudia", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-05-13", text: "We had an excellent trip with Dickies, he was a very knowledgeable and friendly guide. Would definitely recommend to anyone looking to do a Cu Chi tunnels tour." },
                { author: "Dwain", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-03-20", text: "Sunny was a great guide, very informative and friendly, definitely recommended" },
                { author: "Grainne", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-03-19", text: "Talk with war veteran was excellent. Tour guide didn’t seem as enthusiastic as other guides on tours and it felt like she was impatient with us. Also added in an extra trip at the end of the tour on way back to Ho Chi Minh which wasn’t mentioned in the itinerary- we didn’t ended up going on this extra trip due to time constraints for guests" },
                { author: "Sarah", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-03-07", text: "Amazing tour with tein, she went above and beyond for us, bringing us to quieter places and could answer all of our questions! Would 1000% recommend this tour" },
                { author: "Paul", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-02-19", text: "Dickies, our tour guide was excellent with pre-tour info and picked us up nice and early from our hotel so we were one of the first groups at the tunnels - it was getting v busy as we left so an early start was a good call. Dickies managed my question assault about the history of the war and Vietnamese life in general beautifully despite having a sore throat and for that we're grateful and thankful. His english is excellent and he helped explain the exhibits once we were there and the entire half day was really educational and informative, packing a lot in. Had a tour of a factory where people" },
                { author: "Ryan", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-01-18", text: "Really excellent experience that I’d recommend to anyone in Ho Chi Minh, made all the more better by Sunny our tour guide (apologies if I’ve spelt that wrong!) who was very chatty, knowledgable and helpful. The tour does arrive back in Saigon at 3:30pm (not 1pm)." },
                { author: "Martijn", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-11-20", text: "David the tourguide was a great guide. Cu Chi Tunnels are super crowded thats a bit a pity." },
                { author: "Jennifer", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-11-18", text: "It was a really nice tour and the place is managing well with the large amount of tourists coming there. The war veteran however only speaks Vietnamese and will only be with you for a short amount of time, not actually guiding the tour." },
                { author: "Florian", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-11-14", text: "Our friendly tour guide Dickie gave us a lot of informations about Vietnam, the history of the war and at the cu chi tunnel. Driving was all fine on a spacious minibus. Can absolutely recommend the trip." }
            ]
        },
